  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guardians of the Heart of the World. Strengthening the processes of integral protection in the SNSM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to is to strengthen the research, communication and political advocacy capacities of the Youth and Communications Commissions of the OWYBT (Wiwa indigenous organisation) and the Women&apos;s Commission of the OIK (Kankuamo indigenous organisation), so that they can demand that their ethnic and territorial rights are respected and a comprehensive protection of the Heart of the World from an integral ecology, ethnic revitalisation and women&apos;s empowerment approach. The project will be implemented in the Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta, which is considered the Heart of the World by the Peoples of the Sierra. 
Strategies to achieve this include 1) Strengthening of local capacities for the integral care and protection of the Heart of the World and its inhabitants. 2) Awareness raising and communication of the Heart of the World Appeal. 3) Advocacy to share the Heart of the World Appeal.</narrative>
  </description>
